    text: 'Errors use the HTTP status and a JSON body:\n\n```json\n{ "statusCode": 404, "error": "Not Found", "message": "Product not found" }\n```\n\n| Status  | Meaning                                                                                                         |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **400** | Invalid input. `message` is a list with one entry per problem (see below).                                      |\n| **401** | The key or token is missing, wrong, revoked or expired.                                                         |\n| **402** | The plan doesn\'t allow it. The body adds a machine-readable `code`, the `feature`, `plan`, `limit` and `usage`. |\n| **403** | The role lacks the permission.                                                                                  |\n| **404** | Not found, or not in this workspace.                                                                            |\n| **409** | Conflicts with existing data, such as a duplicate SKU or handle.                                                |\n| **429** | Too many requests (see rate limits).                                                            |\n| **5xx** | A server problem. Safe requests (`GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`) can be retried with backoff.                           |\n\nA `400` lists every problem:\n\n```json\n{\n  "statusCode": 400,\n  "error": "Bad Request",\n  "message": ["title should not be empty", "variants must contain at least 1 elements"]\n}\n```\n\nA `402` has `code` set to `plan_limit_reached` or `plan_feature_not_included`, plus the `feature`,\nthe `plan`, its `limit` and current `usage`, so you can tell the user what to upgrade.',
